From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howeasy <howardabudd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:01:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] slink: Polished Crystal 3.2.3 handler, cut 1 (load + lossless
 save, no writers)

PolishedCrystalRomHandler, a sibling of Gen2RomHandler: exact detection
(PKPC, version 50, non-Japanese, header checksum 0xA36C, 2 MiB), 291
species + 46 variant forms as BaseData records 1..337 (stride 34), the
renumbered type ids, the 8-byte moves, evolutions and learnsets
(read-only). Save writes back only the base-stat and move fields the model
owns, so an all-off run is byte-identical. Every setter throws; names are
placeholders. Registered in the CLI and GUI handler arrays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FORK_CHANGES.md                               |  11 +
 .../dabomstew/pkrandom/cli/CliRandomizer.java |   1 +
 .../pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini      | 723 +++++++++++++
 .../pkrandom/constants/PolishedConstants.java |  67 ++
 .../pkrandom/newgui/NewRandomizerGUI.java     |   1 +
 .../PolishedCrystalRomHandler.java            | 946 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1749 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini
 create mode 100644 src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/constants/PolishedConstants.java
 create mode 100644 src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/romhandlers/PolishedCrystalRomHandler.java

diff --git a/FORK_CHANGES.md b/FORK_CHANGES.md
index fde8b82..8c8d2b5 100644
--- a/FORK_CHANGES.md
+++ b/FORK_CHANGES.md
@@ -103,3 +103,14 @@ entries), so a vanilla `[Red (U)]`-style entry executes exactly the original cod
   for the SLink companion-overlay builds (header CRCs 0xD3B7 / 0x0D7E / 0x0B94; banks 0/1/3 shifted).
   Without them the exact-CRC lookup missed and the generic fallback chose the VANILLA Red/Blue entry.
   `StarterOffsets1/2` gain the HallOfFame `cp STARTER1`/`cp STARTER2` operands (postgame ball-hide branch).
+
+## Patch 16 — Polished Crystal 3.2.3 handler, cut 1 (load + lossless save, no writers)
+- `romhandlers/PolishedCrystalRomHandler.java` (new, sibling of `Gen2RomHandler`): exact detection on
+  game code `PKPC` + version + non-Japanese + header checksum (no wildcard) + 2 MiB; reads 291 species
+  and the 46 variant forms (`VariantSpeciesAndFormTable`) as BaseData records 1..337 (stride 34), the
+  renumbered types, the 8-byte moves, evolutions and learnsets. Save writes back only the base-stat and
+  move fields it owns, so an all-off run is byte-identical. Every setter throws; names are placeholders.
+- `constants/PolishedConstants.java` (new): type table, record layouts, 2-byte species decoding.
+- `config/polished_offsets.ini` (new): the block spliced by SLink's `tools/gen_upr_polished_ini.py --fork`
+  plus a hand-kept supplement (Version, CRCInHeader, variant table) the generator does not emit yet.
+- `cli/CliRandomizer.java`, `newgui/NewRandomizerGUI.java`: the factory joins both handler arrays.
diff --git a/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/cli/CliRandomizer.java b/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/cli/CliRandomizer.java
index 6ac0abc..6c34033 100644
--- a/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/cli/CliRandomizer.java
+++ b/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/cli/CliRandomizer.java
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ public class CliRandomizer {
         RomHandler.Factory[] checkHandlers = new RomHandler.Factory[] {
                 new Gen1RomHandler.Factory(),
                 new Gen2RomHandler.Factory(),
+                new PolishedCrystalRomHandler.Factory(),
                 new Gen3RomHandler.Factory(),
                 new Gen4RomHandler.Factory(),
                 new Gen5RomHandler.Factory(),
